---

# 4.7 DEPENDENCY PRINCIPLE

Every engine should depend only on the information it genuinely requires.

Avoid:

Hidden Dependencies

Circular Dependencies

Duplicate Responsibilities

Every dependency should be explicitly documented before implementation begins.

---

# 4.8 INTEGRATION PRINCIPLE

Modules should integrate through standardized interfaces.

Every engine should know:

What it receives

What it produces

Where it sends its output

No engine should directly interfere with another engine's internal logic.

---

# 4.9 IMPLEMENTATION VALIDATION

Implementation is considered incomplete until the module has been validated.

Validation includes:

Logic Validation

↓

Input Validation

↓

Output Validation

↓

Integration Validation

↓

Stress Testing

↓

Documentation Review

Only validated modules become operational.

