---

# 4.13 IMPLEMENTATION SUCCESS CRITERIA

An implementation is considered successful when it is:

Correct

Reliable

Repeatable

Explainable

Reusable

Maintainable

Scalable

Institutional Grade

Implementation is not measured by the amount of code written.

Implementation is measured by the quality of the operating system produced.

